SECURITY TOOLING NOTICE - READ BEFORE USE
===============================================================================

This repository contains WORKING ATTACK TOOLING. The scripts in attack/
simulate payment card fraud - bulk testing of card numbers against a checkout
form (OWASP Automated Threat OAT-001 "Carding") and brute-forcing a card's
expiry and security code (OAT-010 "Card Cracking").

It exists for one purpose: to demonstrate, in a controlled laboratory, how a
web application firewall defends a payment form against those attacks.

AUTHORISED USE ONLY
    Run these tools only against systems you own, or for which you hold
    explicit written permission to conduct security testing. Unauthorised
    access to a computer system is a criminal offence in most jurisdictions,
    including under the US Computer Fraud and Abuse Act and the UK Computer
    Misuse Act 1990. Testing a third party's payment form without authorisation
    may additionally constitute payment fraud.

NO REAL CARDHOLDER DATA
    Every card number these tools generate is synthetic, built against
    published sandbox BIN ranges. The "issuer" they talk to is a local fake
    that approves cards based on an HMAC of a lab secret; it has no connection
    to any payment network and its verdicts are meaningless anywhere else.

    Never supply real cardholder data to this software. The bundled application
    is deliberately insecure, stores data in memory in the clear, and is not
    PCI-DSS compliant. It must never be used to process genuine payments.

DELIBERATELY VULNERABLE APPLICATION
    The application in app/ is intentionally unprotected: no rate limiting, no
    bot detection, no CSRF token, and deliberately informative decline codes.
    Do not deploy it on a public network without a web application firewall in
    front of it or a network ACL restricting access to it.

